PURPOSE Load regular and same-day orders into the paper's epoch-specific dataset.
INPUT case directory, row/ID selection, parsing and model configuration
OUTPUT orders, physical vehicles, future arrivals and input provenance
REFERENCES Program.GetCoordTWDic_Dy; GetTsOrNotandRideshareOrNot

PROCEDURE LoadCase(directory,selection,config)
    resolve vehicle coordinate/window, static-order coordinate/window,
        dynamic-order coordinate/window and transfer/sharing-flag inputs
    resolve explicitly configured LT schedules and fixed-route inputs, if used
    read headers and rows using the declared delimiter/culture/schema
    check finite coordinates, unique IDs, valid windows and matched row identities
    pair coordinates/windows by ID; for row-indexed files verify row IDs first
    apply selection consistently to both coordinate/window records
    FOR each physical vehicle k
        create origin, return point, type ADR/LT, zone, capacity and duty limit
        record availability, mode-specific travel/cost data and optional schedule
    FOR each order r
        create one stable order ID, type regular/same-day and submission time
        record pickup/delivery windows, locations, size and service eligibility
        attach transfer/sharing permissions and declared unserved penalty
        create r+/r- fragment IDs only as views of this same order
    initialOrders := orders visible at config.initialDecisionTime
    arrivals := remaining orders sorted by (submittedAt,stableOrderId)
    check that all required cost weights, durations and time-grid rules are set
    return InputDataset{orders:initialOrders,vehicles,arrivals,
                        selectedFiles,configuration:config}

PROCEDURE ReadArrivals(arrivals,decisionTime,seenIds)
    records := all records with submittedAt <= decisionTime and ID not in seenIds
    return records, seenIds union IDs(records)

PROCEDURE OrdersForEpoch(knownOrders,previousPlan,decisionTime)
    retain previously accepted unfinished orders as mandatory service
    include visible pending/unserved orders with a remaining admissible window
    exclude completed service from new demand while retaining its committed history
    classify expired requests explicitly; do not silently remove accepted work
    return mandatory, optional, completed, expired

PROCEDURE CopyIdentity(original,newRole)
    copy all identity/metadata fields; set newRole before dictionary insertion
    return immutable record

NOTES
    The input schema declares IDs, capacities, duty limits, travel/cost data and
    arrival times. Header-only dynamic inputs represent a static case.
    Case filenames do not determine model parameters.
